   "source": [
    "# RAG 8 Architectures: Complete Taxonomy and Examples\n",
    "\n",
    "This Jupyter notebook provides a comprehensive overview of the 8 primary RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) architectural patterns, each with detailed explanations and practical examples. These architectures represent different approaches to combining retrieval systems with generative AI to enhance language model capabilities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Classic RAG Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: The foundational RAG pattern that retrieves relevant documents and passes them as context to the language model for generation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Vector database for storing embeddings\n",
    "- Dense vector similarity search (embedders)\n",
    "- LLM for generation\n",
    "- Context augmentation pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: General question answering, document Q&A, knowledge base applications\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Simplified Classic RAG implementation\nclass ClassicRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, llm):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.llm = llm\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Create query embedding\n        query_embedding = self.embedder.embed(query)\n        \n        # Retrieve similar documents\n        similar_docs = self.vector_db.similarity_search(\n            query_embedding, k=5\n        )\n        \n        # Augment prompt with retrieved context\n        context = "\\n\\n".join(doc.page_content for doc in similar_docs)\n        prompt = f\"Context:\\n{context}\\\\n\\nQuestion: {query}\"
        \n        # Generate response\n        return self.llm.generate(prompt)\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Conditional RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG variant that uses query analysis to determine whether to retrieve or rely on the model's existing knowledge.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Query classifier or router\n",
    "- Two response paths (retrieve vs. no-retrieve)\n",
    "- Adaptive context management\n",
    "- Performance optimization layer\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Efficiency optimization, reducing unnecessary retrieval costs\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Conditional RAG implementation\nclass ConditionalRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, llm, knowledge_cutoff_date):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.knowledge_cutoff_date = knowledge_cutoff_date\n        self.query_classifier = QueryClassifier()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Analyze if retrieval is needed\n        retrieval_needed = self.query_classifier.should_retrieve(query)\n        \n        if retrieval_needed:\n            # Get current knowledge\n            query_embedding = self.embedder.embed(query)\n            docs = self.vector_db.similarity_search(query_embedding, k=5)\n            context = self._format_context(docs)\n        else:\n            # Use model knowledge only\n            context = self._get_knowledge_limit_notice()\n        \n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Multi-Vector RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: Advanced RAG that uses multiple vector representations and retrieval strategies to improve result quality.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Multiple embedding models\n",
    "- Hybrid vector search (dense + sparse)\n",
    "- Cross-encoder reranking\n",
    "- Multi-stage retrieval pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: High-precision retrieval tasks, complex semantic matching\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Multi-Vector RAG implementation\nclass MultiVectorRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, llm):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.dense_embedder = DenseEmbedder()\n        self.sparse_embedder = SparseEmbedder()\n        self.cross_encoder = CrossEncoderReranker()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Create multiple representations\n        dense_vec = self.dense_embedder.embed(query)\n        sparse_vec = self.sparse_embedder.embed(query)\n        \n        # Hybrid search\n        results = self.vector_db.hybrid_search(dense_vec, sparse_vec, k=20)\n        \n        # Rerank with cross-encoder\n        reranked_results = self.cross_encoder.rerank(query, results)\n        \n        # Format final context\n        context = self._format_context(reranked_results[:5])\n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. GraphRAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG that leverages knowledge graphs to capture relationships between entities and improve context understanding.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Knowledge graph construction\n",
    "- Entity relationship extraction\n",
    "- Graph-based retrieval algorithms\n",
    "- Path-based context aggregation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Complex reasoning, relationship-focused queries, fact-checking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# GraphRAG implementation\nclass GraphRAG:\n    def __init__(self, knowledge_graph, llm):\n        self.knowledge_graph = knowledge_graph\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.entity_extractor = EntityExtractor()\n        self.relation_extractor = RelationExtractor()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Extract entities and relations from query\n        entities = self.entity_extractor.extract(query)\n        relations = self.relation_extractor.extract(query)\n        \n        # Traverse knowledge graph\n        relevant_paths = self.knowledge_graph.find_paths(\n            entities, relations, max_depth=3\n        )\n        \n        # Aggregate contextual information\n        context = self._aggregate_graph_context(relevant_paths)\n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Document-GRAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG optimized for document processing, incorporating document structure and metadata into the retrieval process.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Document parser and OCR\n",
    "- Document structure analysis\n",
    "- Metadata-aware retrieval\n",
    "- Section-level context aggregation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Legal documents, academic papers, structured text processing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Document-GRAG implementation\nclass DocumentRAG:\n    def __init__(self, document_processor, llm):\n        self.document_processor = document_processor\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.section_analyzer = SectionAnalyzer()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Process documents with structure awareness\n        processed_docs = self.document_processor.process_all("document_collection")\n        \n        # Analyze document sections relevant to query\n        relevant_sections = self.section_analyzer.find_relevant_sections(\n            processed_docs, query\n        )\n        \n        # Context from specific document sections\n        context = self._format_document_context(relevant_sections)\n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Memory-Augmented RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG that maintains persistent memory of previous interactions to improve context continuity and personalization.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Short-term memory buffer\n",
    "- Long-term memory storage\n",
    "- Conversation context management\n",
    "- Memory-aware context merging\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Conversational AI, personalized assistants, multi-turn conversations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Memory-Augmented RAG implementation\nclass MemoryAugmentedRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, llm, memory_system):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.memory_system = memory_system\n        self.context_manager = ContextManager()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Retrieve relevant documents\n        query_embedding = self.embedder.embed(query)\n        docs = self.vector_db.similarity_search(query_embedding, k=5)\n        \n        # Get conversation memory\n        conversation_memory = self.memory_system.get_recent_context(query, window=10)\n        \n        # Merge context intelligently\n        merged_context = self.context_manager.merge_context(\n            docs, conversation_memory\n        )\n        \n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{merged_context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Self-RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG that uses the generation itself to assess confidence and potentially trigger additional retrieval.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Confidence estimation\n",
    "- Self-assessment mechanisms\n",
    "- Dynamic retrieval triggers\n",
    "- Confidence-aware response generation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Uncertainty quantification, confidence-based retrieval, error reduction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Self-RAG implementation\nclass SelfRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, llm, confidence_estimator):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.llm = llm\n        self.confidence_estimator = confidence_estimator\n        self.additional_retriever = AdditionalRetriever()\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Initial retrieval\n        query_embedding = self.embedder.embed(query)\n        docs = self.vector_db.similarity_search(query_embedding, k=5)\n        context = self._format_context(docs)\n        \n        # Generate with confidence assessment\n        response = self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n        confidence = self.confidence_estimator.estimate(response, query)\n        \n        # Trigger additional retrieval if confidence is low\n        if confidence < 0.7:\n            additional_docs = self.additional_retriever.fetch_additional(query, docs)\n            enhanced_context = context + "\\n" + self._format_context(additional_docs)\n            return self.llm.generate(f\"{enhanced_context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n        \n        return response\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Sparse-Retrieval RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "**Description**: RAG that uses keyword-based or sparse retrieval methods in conjunction with dense vector search.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Components**:\n",
    "- Sparse vector embeddings\n",
    "- Keyword-based indexing\n",
    "- BM25 or TF-IDF search\n",
    "- Hybrid dense-sparse retrieval\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use Case**: Exact keyword matching, hybrid search systems, complementary retrieval\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**:\n",
    "```python\n# Sparse-Retrieval RAG implementation\nclass SparseRetrievalRAG:\n    def __init__(self, vector_db, bm25_index, llm):\n        self.vector_db = vector_db\n        self.bm25_index = bm25_index\n        self.llm = llm\n    \n    def retrieve_and_generate(self, query):\n        # Parallel sparse and dense retrieval\n        dense_results = self._dense_retrieval(query)\n        sparse_results = self.bm25_index.search(query, k=10)\n        \n        # Cross-referencing and deduplication\n        combined_results = self._combine_results(dense_results, sparse_results)\n        \n        # Final ranking\n        ranked_results = self._rank_results(query, combined_results)\n        \n        context = self._format_context(ranked_results[:5])\n        return self.llm.generate(f\"{context}\\n\\n{query}\")\n```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Architecture Selection Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "Each RAG architecture serves different use cases. Choose based on:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Performance vs. Accuracy Trade-offs**:\n",
    "- Classic RAG: Best balance of performance and accuracy\n",
    "- Conditional RAG: Optimized for latency-sensitive applications\n",
    "- Multi-Vector RAG: Highest accuracy, premium performance\n",
    "- GraphRAG: Best for relationship-heavy data\n",
    "- Document-GRAG: Ideal for structured documents\n",
    "- Memory-Augmented RAG: Best for conversational applications\n",
    "- Self-RAG: Excellent for confidence-aware systems\n",
    "- Sparse-Retrieval RAG: Perfect for hybrid search needs\n",
    "\n",
    "**Implementation Considerations**:\n",
    "- Data characteristics (structured vs. unstructured)\n",
    "- Performance requirements (latency, throughput)\n",
    "- Available infrastructure (memory, storage)\n",
    "- Accuracy requirements (precision, recall)\n",
    "- User experience expectations\n"
   ]
  }
